}

::CW_U03_L04_Q19::[MLA.CW.WR.01] Passage: Kai wants to be seen as brave, so he hides his shaking hands in his pockets before stepping forward. Central idea: Courage can exist beside fear. What detail supports it?{
~A. Kai has pockets.#Incorrect. Pockets matter only because they hide fear.
~B. Kai never moves.#Incorrect. He steps forward. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
~C. Kai feels no fear.#Incorrect. His hands shake. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
=D. Kai steps forward while hiding shaking hands.#Correct. The action shows fear and courage together.
}

::CW_U03_L04_Q20::[MLA.CW.WR.01] Which revision best supports "kindness can interrupt cruelty"?{
