~C. Add a weather report.#Incorrect. Weather does not support the idea by itself.
~D. Remove the harmed student.#Incorrect. That weakens the conflict. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
}

::CW_U03_L04_Q21::[MLA.CW.WR.01] Central idea: Letting go can be an act of care. Which detail supports it?{
~A. The character locks the cage tighter.#Incorrect. That works against letting go. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
~B. The character paints a wall.#Incorrect. Unrelated. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
=C. The character gives the injured bird space after opening the cage door.#Correct. Letting the bird go shows care. This answer matches the lesson skill and is supported by the specific creative-writing evidence in the prompt.
