}

::CW_U03_L04_Q22::[MLA.CW.WR.01] Which explanation is strongest? Central idea: Secrets can damage trust. Detail: The character deletes a message before her friend sees it.{
=A. The deleted message supports the idea because hiding communication creates secrecy between friends.#Correct. It explains how evidence connects to trust.
~B. It supports the idea because it is a sentence.#Incorrect. Being a sentence is not enough. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
~C. It supports the idea because phones exist.#Incorrect. The phone is not the main connection.
~D. It does not matter what details do.#Incorrect. Details must connect to the central idea.
}

::CW_U03_L04_Q23::[MLA.CW.WR.01] Central idea: Persistence means trying again with a wiser plan. Which detail best supports it?{
~A. The character repeats the same mistake without thinking.#Incorrect. That lacks a wiser plan. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
~B. The character quits immediately.#Incorrect. That does not show persistence. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
~C. The character names the river only.#Incorrect. Naming alone is not development. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
